	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Tirisfal Glades was once the heart of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. Its long green valleys fed the greatest of the human kingdoms, and on its eastern edge stood the kingdom's {link:capital-city}Capital City{/link}. Now the glades are grey. Mist hangs over empty farms, the mills turn for no one, and the crows are fat. The land belongs to the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}, the dead who woke to their own minds again. From {link:brill}Brill{/link} and the {link:undercity}Undercity{/link} they hold it against the living and the dead alike.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records the year when the first settlers came to Tirisfal. They came from {link:arathor}Arathor{/link}, in the long centuries after the {link:troll-wars}Troll Wars{/link}, and they found rich soil and quiet forests. Their farmsteads grew into a kingdom, and that kingdom took the name of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. In later ages, noble families from the old {link:arathi-highlands}Arathi{/link} heartland bought great estates in the glades. The Agamands, who owned the mills of the northern highlands, were counted the most prosperous of them all.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} of {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas Windrunner{/link} rule Tirisfal, but they rule a land at war. The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} still holds the {link:agamand-mills}Agamand Mills{/link} and slips past the {link:the-bulwark}Bulwark{/link}, the wall that guards the glades from the Plaguelands to the east. The {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} marches out of its monastery in the north-east and keeps watchtowers across the land. {link:gnolls}Gnolls{/link} rob the mass graves for corpses to feed the Lich King's armies. In the capital, the {link:royal-apothecary-society}Royal Apothecary Society{/link} works on a new plague, and the Deathguard keep living prisoners in the cellar of a tavern until the apothecaries have need of them.

New troubles have come as well. Not long ago the necropolis {red:naxxramas}Naxxramas{/red} struck at the {link:undercity}Undercity{/link}, and the shards of its great crystal still lie scattered in the fields near the ruined capital, where the {link:cult-of-the-damned}Cult of the Damned{/link} hunts for them. In the western mountains, a new order of Forsaken paladins keeps a fortress of its own. Few of their people trust them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}.{/b} The Deathguard patrol the roads, the executors give the orders, and the newly risen wake in the crypt of {link:deathknell}Deathknell{/link} every day.
• {b}The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}.{/b} Mindless dead, skeletons and necromancers still infest the mills, the farms and the old crypts.
• {b}The {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link}.{/b} Zealots in red who burn every undead they find, whether it serves the Lich King or not.
• {b}The Rot Hide gnolls.{/b} Slaves of the Scourge who dig up the dead.
• {b}{link:murlocs}Murlocs{/link} and beasts.{/b} The Vile Fin tribes of the coast and lakes, darkhounds, duskbats and the great spiders of the eastern vales.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Plague.{/b} In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, the plague of the {link:cult-of-the-damned}Cult of the Damned{/link} swept the glades. Whole families died and rose again as {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}.
• {b}The Fall.{/b} Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} murdered his father {link:terenas-menethil}Terenas Menethil{/link} in his own throne room. The capital fell, and Tirisfal fell with it. That was the {link:fall-of-lordaeron}Fall of Lordaeron{/link}.
• {b}The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}.{/b} When the Lich King's grip weakened, {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas{/link} and her followers broke free and claimed the ruins of the capital. Beneath it they built the {link:undercity}Undercity{/link}.
• {b}The Necropolis.{/b} When Naxxramas came against the Undercity, the Forsaken fought it on the surface. The {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link} fought beside them, and many fell.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Glades",
			text = [=[• The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} say that the crypt-keepers of {link:deathknell}Deathknell{/link} were ready to burn many of the new risen before they woke.
• Before the plague, the reclusive folk of {link:shadowvale}Shadowvale{/link} brewed a green elixir from herbs of the western hills. It was sought by apothecaries, mystics and poisoners alike, even after it was forbidden in the capital.]=],
		},
	},
})

